{
  "message": "I’m sorry, but I can’t cancel reservation H9ZU1C under the cancellation rules I have. I confirmed both flight segments are still available/not flown, but the reservation was created on 2024-05-01, is economy, has no travel insurance, and the flights were not cancelled by the airline. Since your reason is effectively a change of plan/rebooking later, it does not meet the listed cancellation conditions: booking within the last 24 hours, airline-cancelled flight, business flight, or covered travel-insurance cancellation. [airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-cancel-flight]\n\nBecause the policy says the cancellation API does not check these rules and I must make sure they apply before calling it, I can’t proceed with cancellation for H9ZU1C. [airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-cancel-flight]"
}

{
  "message": "I’m really sorry, but based on the reservation details I found, I can’t process this cancellation with a full refund through our standard cancellation tool. Your reservation PEP4E0 is for a one-way basic economy trip from CLT to PHX, paid by credit card for $128, with no travel insurance, and the flights are currently listed as available/not flown. Under the cancellation policy, a flight can be cancelled for refund only if the booking was made within the last 24 hours, the airline cancelled the flight, it is a business flight, or the user has travel insurance and the reason is covered. Your stated reason is “other reasons” for a family emergency, the reservation is basic economy, has no insurance, and I don’t see an airline cancellation. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-cancel-flight. I understand this is stressful and urgent. Since I’m not able to approve an exception or full refund under the available policy/tools, I can transfer you to a human agent to review whether any exception is possible."
}

{
  "message": "I understand, and I won’t transfer you since you asked me not to. I also can’t escalate or approve an exception myself without transferring to a human agent; that option isn’t available to me through the tools I have. Under the cancellation policy, I can only cancel for refund if one of these applies: the booking was made within the last 24 hours, the airline cancelled the flight, it is a business flight, or the reservation has travel insurance and the reason is covered. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-cancel-flight. Your reservation shows basic economy, no travel insurance, and the flight statuses I checked are available rather than airline-cancelled. Source for flight status meanings: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-domain-basic-flight. I don’t have a separate current-time tool, so I can’t independently verify the 24-hour booking window beyond the reservation creation timestamp shown in the system. If you believe the booking was made within the last 24 hours, please tell me and I can reassess. Otherwise, I’m sorry, but I can’t process a full-refund cancellation for this reservation under the policy."
}

{
  "message": "I’m sorry, but I can’t change the flight date for this reservation. Your reservation PEP4E0 is in basic economy, and the modify-flight policy says basic economy flights cannot be modified. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-modify-flight. I also won’t transfer you since you asked me not to. The only modification potentially allowed for basic economy is changing cabin without changing the flights, if no flight has already been flown, but that would not move the trip to May 22nd. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-modify-flight."
}

{
  "message": "I’m sorry, but I can’t add travel insurance to an existing reservation. I don’t have an available tool or policy authorization that allows me to add insurance after booking, so I can’t use that as a way to make the reservation eligible for cancellation now. The cancellation policy only allows cancellation/refund when one of the listed conditions applies, including that the user already has travel insurance and the reason is covered; your reservation details show insurance is “no.” Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-cancel-flight. I also understand you don’t want a cabin upgrade or a transfer, so I won’t do either. Based on the options available to me, I’m not able to cancel for a full refund, change the date, or add insurance to make it refundable."
}

{
  "message": "I won’t proceed at $396. Based on the available economy prices for the existing flights, I don’t see a way to upgrade OWZ4XL to economy within your $100 total budget.

I also can’t apply an exception or waiver from here: the supplied policy allows cabin changes for basic economy only when flights have not been flown, but it does not provide a medical/emergency waiver process or authority for me to override the fare difference. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-modify-flight. Claims about possible medical waivers are therefore not covered by the supplied sources.

Because OWZ4XL is currently basic economy, I also can’t change the flights themselves to the nonstop unless the cabin is changed first; policy says basic economy flights cannot be modified. Source: airline/policy.md:airline-agent-policy-modify-flight.

If you’d like, I can transfer you to a human agent to ask whether any off-policy hardship or medical exception is available."
}

{
  "message": "You’re being transferred to a human agent now. I included the details of your reservation, the nonstop option, your $100 maximum budget, and your request for a hardship/medical exception due to your mother’s illness."
}

